[{:db/id "q-104586/selection/07496f5e0a7a84e39f443c761d27aef9c935e34660bb7a2513e1f14c637f8003" :answer/id #uuid "cb18b8a6-ff14-57fc-8477-3b7ce148d6c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(t+1)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104586/selection/ec0ffc1c2a2a91c50875f71d7bce369e099ea8dce25d75816a27e5aac054db94" :answer/id #uuid "23a3e6c3-8292-523b-9e36-f4facb6d998b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3t+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104586/selection/cd1fa96755d46eaa857b7cb8136c5c1f86ee0b589ee60b94ceb232007f90fba6" :answer/id #uuid "0378fa66-0a05-5010-947f-e286b08defeb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(t+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104586/selection/1c9f48e873294f7a88271e625df41c9a200057c35e4d832d7b5ddc7c6c0955d9" :answer/id #uuid "233d3af3-86cc-5bf9-b5d7-de96e4ef3492" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2t+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104586/selection/7fc76acb28f938faf8ffe7fc54f0c0321b7f28cd2bbbabfdc6a620bf80cb5176" :answer/id #uuid "f18c9102-c7c1-56a0-ba8c-83ff21cf67cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104586/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0328331-ae0b-5500-84bc-6aa536a3b471" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104586/selection/cd1fa96755d46eaa857b7cb8136c5c1f86ee0b589ee60b94ceb232007f90fba6" :answer-field/choices ["q-104586/selection/07496f5e0a7a84e39f443c761d27aef9c935e34660bb7a2513e1f14c637f8003" "q-104586/selection/ec0ffc1c2a2a91c50875f71d7bce369e099ea8dce25d75816a27e5aac054db94" "q-104586/selection/cd1fa96755d46eaa857b7cb8136c5c1f86ee0b589ee60b94ceb232007f90fba6" "q-104586/selection/1c9f48e873294f7a88271e625df41c9a200057c35e4d832d7b5ddc7c6c0955d9" "q-104586/selection/7fc76acb28f938faf8ffe7fc54f0c0321b7f28cd2bbbabfdc6a620bf80cb5176"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104586" :question/id #uuid "b4d357cf-ef8c-58b5-a035-2c81e0202dd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-104586" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t],$ the vector space of polynomials of degree at most $2$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nfind the orthogonal projection of $p(t)=5{t}^{2}$ onto the subspace spanned by $q(t)=t+1.$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $p(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{q(t)}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t)=\\frac{⟨p(t),q(t)⟩}{⟨q(t),q(t)⟩}\\,q(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1) \\\\  & =(5{t}^{2}){|}_{-1}\\,\\cdot \\,(t\\,+\\,1){|}_{-1}+(5{t}^{2}){|}_{0}\\,\\cdot \\,(t\\,+\\,1){|}_{0}+(5{t}^{2}){|}_{1}\\,\\cdot \\,(t\\,+\\,1){|}_{1} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1+5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =0+0+10 \\\\  & =10,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨q(t),q(t)⟩ & =q(-1)q(-1)+q(0)q(0)+q(1)q(1) \\\\  & =(t\\,+\\,1){|}_{-1}\\,\\cdot \\,(t\\,+\\,1){|}_{-1}+(t\\,+\\,1){|}_{0}\\,\\cdot \\,(t\\,+\\,1){|}_{0}+(t\\,+\\,1){|}_{1}\\,\\cdot \\,(t\\,+\\,1){|}_{1} \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =0+1+4 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the projection is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t) & =\\frac{⟨p(t),q(t)⟩}{⟨q(t),q(t)⟩}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5}\\cdot (t+1) \\\\  & =2(t+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104586/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "df300955-830a-5347-9aeb-2b2b25f865c8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104586"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104862/selection/b77633b0368d8725fb5dcaece4aed8339ab5d3308acf6e8e6f2f935193fda378" :answer/id #uuid "72a857b9-8f83-51a6-ad75-1df44448cbc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104862/selection/e64ed06f41ebee4dc554f931a1f31dc3e011359e9b9395022b1a685743955768" :answer/id #uuid "2c05cce1-6b06-5cd5-b9f0-a77b7b39cc83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2t-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104862/selection/402698786a2196947323809d3a80b73a46d8692651fdfd7bfaed955c55f7637a" :answer/id #uuid "ff22d85f-07ff-5431-bc98-4466989c800b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104862/selection/46dea90cf023e3198ba69cc408a1d1f5662fd1f48dd04eb68771558ef933ec92" :answer/id #uuid "dc242429-6f6e-5f6a-bc1f-6d81bbc28a2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104862/selection/cb9ad14c4d0189695cf5d02baf58f5eec7ac941edc170f6dffed142cbab880f5" :answer/id #uuid "3572edda-f5b7-59ae-aabb-27521d299013" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104862/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ab378581-d34d-5bda-8b76-a1ad90d2814f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104862/selection/402698786a2196947323809d3a80b73a46d8692651fdfd7bfaed955c55f7637a" :answer-field/choices ["q-104862/selection/b77633b0368d8725fb5dcaece4aed8339ab5d3308acf6e8e6f2f935193fda378" "q-104862/selection/e64ed06f41ebee4dc554f931a1f31dc3e011359e9b9395022b1a685743955768" "q-104862/selection/402698786a2196947323809d3a80b73a46d8692651fdfd7bfaed955c55f7637a" "q-104862/selection/46dea90cf023e3198ba69cc408a1d1f5662fd1f48dd04eb68771558ef933ec92" "q-104862/selection/cb9ad14c4d0189695cf5d02baf58f5eec7ac941edc170f6dffed142cbab880f5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104862" :question/id #uuid "0145917b-7e1e-5e24-aaa7-e9966e74c556" :question/math-academy-id "q-104862" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t],$ the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nfind the orthogonal projection of $p(t)=2{t}^{2}-2t$ onto the subspace spanned by $q(t)=2t.$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $p(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{q(t)}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t)=\\frac{⟨p(t),q(t)⟩}{⟨q(t),q(t)⟩}\\,q(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1) \\\\  & =(2{t}^{2}\\,-\\,2t){|}_{-1}\\,\\cdot \\,(2t){|}_{-1}+(2{t}^{2}\\,-\\,2t){|}_{0}\\,\\cdot \\,(2t){|}_{0}+(2{t}^{2}\\,-\\,2t){|}_{1}\\,\\cdot \\,(2t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-8+0+0 \\\\  & =-8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨q(t),q(t)⟩ & =q(-1)q(-1)+q(0)q(0)+q(1)q(1) \\\\  & =(2t){|}_{-1}\\,\\cdot \\,(2t){|}_{-1}+(2t){|}_{0}\\,\\cdot \\,(2t){|}_{0}+(2t){|}_{1}\\,\\cdot \\,(2t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4+0+4 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the projection is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t) & =\\frac{⟨p(t),q(t)⟩}{⟨q(t),q(t)⟩}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{-8}{8}\\cdot (2t) \\\\  & =-2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104862/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "df300955-830a-5347-9aeb-2b2b25f865c8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104862"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104583/selection/27b9f22655ccf0b2d6755453458dea824e4c0dc7d52ad15a7b9beb5a52a87b8d" :answer/id #uuid "94893112-353f-56f0-90d6-d4c99de1224a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104583/selection/fd9ca1cffa6c209ad15d1b41275c6e3e6bad8553b556d2cb6c937eaaac748dec" :answer/id #uuid "2f9f2ca0-ddf5-557e-bf67-8e1db1f8ea99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104583/selection/46dea90cf023e3198ba69cc408a1d1f5662fd1f48dd04eb68771558ef933ec92" :answer/id #uuid "2f959e56-f894-5809-af2c-2eebe7633db1" :answer/type :answer.